                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5165620f-6ad6-34e2-8291-622462eae313",
                        "entry_id": "73f39408-e5b9-3bd5-b6c7-c5d1a68d86e2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Schnapstrinker oder Alkoholiker"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4bb07c5f-6585-42d3-bd49-bd0ace1cf9bc",
                                "sense_id": "5165620f-6ad6-34e2-8291-622462eae313",
                                "text": "Der Kioskbesitzer ist ja im ganzen Viertel als Schnapsdrossel bekannt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0dad8086-8730-4b41-8b89-8120a45e854f",
                                "sense_id": "5165620f-6ad6-34e2-8291-622462eae313",
                                "text": "Oma war eine Schnapsdrossel, sie hatte in jeder Lebenslage ein Likörchen zur Hand."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0a3730d2-72c8-3d55-89df-d9e4fb7a31a9",
                        "entry_id": "73f39408-e5b9-3bd5-b6c7-c5d1a68d86e2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "jemand, der für ein paar Schnäpse Verdächtige oder Täter verrät"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef2014aa-6a5b-42c1-baaa-a0914ec05edc",
                                "sense_id": "0a3730d2-72c8-3d55-89df-d9e4fb7a31a9",
                                "text": "„Erwin ist keine Schnapsdrossel, die für Schnaps oder einen Schuss die Freunde verrät. Das unterscheidet ihn von Pedro, denn dass der eine Sackratte ist, pfeifen bereits die Spatzen von den Dächern.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95ac72b2-84b2-41c6-b123-88acc8dad17e",
                        "source_entry_id": "73f39408-e5b9-3bd5-b6c7-c5d1a68d86e2",
                        "source_sense_id": "5165620f-6ad6-34e2-8291-622462eae313",
                        "source_sense_description": "scherzhaft: Schnapstrinker oder Alkoholiker",
                        "target_lang_word": "boozer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "boozer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0cf29b47-d765-3c42-896b-953e990d6b79",
                                        "entry_id": "83eca981-4f15-3163-aa3d-53fa0ac36bb8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who drinks alcohol habitually; a drunkard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01fa2bcf-f881-408b-9192-e2e3f7e9f7fb",
                                                "sense_id": "0cf29b47-d765-3c42-896b-953e990d6b79",
                                                "text": "“Tess is a fine figure o′ fun, as I said to myself today when I zeed her vamping round parish with the rest,” observed one of the elderly boozers in an undertone."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e4d5e5e-bfce-41df-87a2-4b82aeace8f6",
                                                "sense_id": "0cf29b47-d765-3c42-896b-953e990d6b79",
                                                "text": "But they have only one insurance rate for ordinary men — drinkers and non-drinkers, and they compel the man who doesn′t booze to make up for the extra amount that the boozer should pay."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb7ac8aa-93b7-4689-9691-699451199dfd",
                                                "sense_id": "0cf29b47-d765-3c42-896b-953e990d6b79",
                                                "text": "\"You were actually taking that old boozer seriously.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2db311e5-0569-4681-91e9-84399b2abe26",
                                                "sense_id": "0cf29b47-d765-3c42-896b-953e990d6b79",
                                                "text": "2009 November, Neville Franks, The Lost Boy of the Ozarks, Backpacker, page 82,\nEvery swig made me more relaxed, and happy, and I was definitely a boozer again, and I wondered why I had ever thought I wasn't a boozer and I took another pull and I was going to clap BC on the back and thank him for being such a good hotel manager, and faithful guide, for being my friend, and then I passed out."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a82c93f1-d97c-3094-8dff-e79e95d549b4",
                                        "entry_id": "83eca981-4f15-3163-aa3d-53fa0ac36bb8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A public house, pub."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "UK",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b7ff51a-336d-4f11-b7a0-2a62c4419d43",
                                                "sense_id": "a82c93f1-d97c-3094-8dff-e79e95d549b4",
                                                "text": "Zoe’s dad went to the same boozer every day, a flat-roofed pub on the edge of the estate, with the cross of St George hanging above the door and a ferocious-looking Rottweiler tied up outside."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33d8a1ea-5122-4e30-ad1c-08e725181de5",
                                                "sense_id": "a82c93f1-d97c-3094-8dff-e79e95d549b4",
                                                "text": "During the week, the players were just as likely to be spotted out together in a local pub such as the Four in Hand. It was even known for them to frequent the Marksman off Carters Green, one of the town’s roughest boozers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae99aba4-abab-3b16-b412-14ca41c81777",
                                        "entry_id": "83eca981-4f15-3163-aa3d-53fa0ac36bb8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A World War II fighter radar detector, fitted to British bombers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "611f07b3-146c-36d9-a70e-2ff9a6ffd0d9",
                                        "entry_id": "83eca981-4f15-3163-aa3d-53fa0ac36bb8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vehicle equipped with tanks for supplying water to remote locations."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Africa"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd0f8523-d867-4212-ad44-075b1a140c94",
                                                "sense_id": "611f07b3-146c-36d9-a70e-2ff9a6ffd0d9",
                                                "text": "2010 June 8, Kenya National Assembly Official Record (Hansard), page 2,\nMr. Mututho: Mr. Speaker, Sir, the Assistant Minister should assure the people of Vihiga that they will get a water boozer because the sick people are not party to this complication. Could he assure the people that he can send a boozer in his capacity even if he cannot supply power or a standby generator, so that they can have a small well?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c1356ca-60f4-4436-93cf-99005003b319",
                        "source_entry_id": "73f39408-e5b9-3bd5-b6c7-c5d1a68d86e2",
                        "source_sense_id": "5165620f-6ad6-34e2-8291-622462eae313",
                        "source_sense_description": "scherzhaft: Schnapstrinker oder Alkoholiker",
                        "target_lang_word": "boozehound",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "boozehound",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0c0635f8-67ae-3b17-9381-146566cb7401",
                                        "entry_id": "8ec1b539-9ebd-39d1-9863-ad83efd190fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "alcoholic, drunkard"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "110fdaf4-d7da-4d15-a284-40517359757a",
                                                "sense_id": "0c0635f8-67ae-3b17-9381-146566cb7401",
                                                "text": "A 47-year-old, nondescript boozehound who once programmed computers for the French government, Houellebecq is an unlikely choice as either a literary lion or sacrificial lamb."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a93a4f36-325c-46d7-a5c9-3d0a73193f7f",
                                                "sense_id": "0c0635f8-67ae-3b17-9381-146566cb7401",
                                                "text": "He was also an irresponsible boozehound who habitually ran out on the check in restaurants, even though he must have known it was the waitress who had to pay the bill for such dine-and-dash customers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "589a1897-cfa5-4863-b177-1d78fa215e76",
                        "source_entry_id": "73f39408-e5b9-3bd5-b6c7-c5d1a68d86e2",
                        "source_sense_id": "5165620f-6ad6-34e2-8291-622462eae313",
                        "source_sense_description": "scherzhaft: Schnapstrinker oder Alkoholiker",
                        "target_lang_word": "poivrot",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "poivrot",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ce8c8c2b-6986-3b51-9358-916857ad985e",
                                        "entry_id": "75bde1ba-942a-3033-b389-42a47c10b45b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alcoolique ; ivrogne ; pochard ; soulard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bea2e0f8-e4c9-4138-bc24-edbb84596754",
                                                "sense_id": "ce8c8c2b-6986-3b51-9358-916857ad985e",
                                                "text": "Mon mariage est fini, on m'a tiré dessus et je me coltine un poivrot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50fa801c-66d1-4099-97c5-2c3dbef302f2",
                                                "sense_id": "ce8c8c2b-6986-3b51-9358-916857ad985e",
                                                "text": "Il lui suffira d'interroger l'horizon, de constater qu'aucun sergent de ville, aucun témoin indiscret n'est à portée, et il pourra tout à loisir retourner les poches du poivrot inconscient."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b5ff8ca-6823-41f9-9280-fde18bfd864e",
                                                "sense_id": "ce8c8c2b-6986-3b51-9358-916857ad985e",
                                                "text": "Je n'ai jamais dissimulé l'indulgente sympathie que j'éprouve à l'égard des poivrots. Je n'écris pas «des ivrognes». L'ivrogne est répugnant, abject et malfaisant. Le poivrot est éloquent, jovial, pittoresque; c'est une nature qui s'extériorise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b710336-8dee-4fa8-a9aa-dbd485ca9cd4",
                                                "sense_id": "ce8c8c2b-6986-3b51-9358-916857ad985e",
                                                "text": "Le poivrot se dépêcha de fourrer la bouteille dans sa poche arrière en lançant aux alentours des regards coupables."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71a81f77-7455-48bf-a280-6832964c03ff",
                                                "sense_id": "ce8c8c2b-6986-3b51-9358-916857ad985e",
                                                "text": "P'pa dévisse le bouchon d'une bouteille de whisky. Je reste bouche bée. Je secoue la tête. Je suis trop bête. Il parle en agitant les mains et les têtes des poivrots suivent la bouteille."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "545727d0-3a1c-42aa-bc3b-9c00fe671c92",
                                                "sense_id": "ce8c8c2b-6986-3b51-9358-916857ad985e",
                                                "text": "Sam Arrignon et Paul Amiaud sont les 2 plus gros poivrots de Chavagnes ! Ils n'arrêtent pas de boire ..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
